    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "kf1a4y7",
      "content": "<strong><br></br>5. High Probability Exam Facts</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uj902rk",
      "content": "- Father of Taxonomy – Carolus Linnaeus"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bbs8hly",
      "content": "- Father of Genetics – Gregor Mendel"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wc7ng3j",
      "content": "- Father of Microbiology – Louis Pasteur"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "57a9vgs",
      "content": "- Metal in Chlorophyll – Magnesium"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "994j8ne",
      "content": "- Powerhouse of the Cell – Mitochondria"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hjn5plq",
      "content": "- Suicide Bags of Cell – Lysosomes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oqne03i",
      "content": "- Universal Donor – O negative"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "15nr9lk",
      "content": "- Universal Receiver – AB positive"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vhe6t3k",
      "content": "- Human Chromosomes – 46 (23 pairs)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "kox5xcn",
      "content": "<strong>Levels of Biological Organization</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ujlwugw",
      "content": "Living organisms are organized into different hierarchical levels. These levels help in understanding the complexity of life forms."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "drciapq",
      "content": "- Cell – Basic structural and functional unit of life."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h8zo9sc",
      "content": "- Tissue – Group of similar cells performing a common function."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s6qcfdl",
      "content": "- Organ – Group of tissues working together."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oekgupl",
      "content": "- Organ System – Group of organs performing major body functions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nwzfor7",
      "content": "- Organism – Complete living individual."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qn9240b",
      "content": "- Population – Group of same species living in an area."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "39chj25",
      "content": "- Community – Different populations living together."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3kz9vg0",
      "content": "- Ecosystem – Interaction between living and non-living components."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pmxa7in",
      "content": "- Biosphere – Sum total of all ecosystems on Earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yt4fe7l",
      "content": "<strong><br></br>7. Difference Between Living and Non-Living Things</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "4c206o7",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Living Things</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Non-Living Things</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Show growth and reproduction</p>",
            "<p>Do not grow or reproduce</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Require food and energy</p>",
            "<p>Do not require food</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Respond to stimuli</p>",
            "<p>No response to stimuli</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Perform metabolism</p>",
            "<p>No metabolic activity</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "81zb1a6",
      "content": "<strong><br></br>8. Important Biological Laws and Concepts</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5ecavjr",
      "content": "- Cell Theory – Proposed by Schleiden and Schwann. States that all living organisms are made up of cells and cells are basic units of life."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "noe4pjr",
      "content": "- Theory of Spontaneous Generation – Disproved by Louis Pasteur."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h6qh7p7",
      "content": "- Biogenesis – Life arises from pre-existing life."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hayqxs2",
      "content": "- Homeostasis – Maintenance of stable internal environment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xj807uq",
      "content": "- Use and Disuse Theory – Proposed by Lamarck."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Xylem",
        "Phloem"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Primary Function",
          "Transports water and minerals",
          "Transports food and nutrients"
        ],
        [
          "Direction of Flow",
          "Unidirectional (Roots to leaves)",
          "Bidirectional (Leaves to all parts)"
        ],
        [
          "Tissue Condition",
          "Mainly composed of dead cells",
          "Mainly composed of living cells"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "1160a3w"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "cd51tqs",
      "content": "<strong><br></br>9. Rules of Binomial Nomenclature</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b7dvmrm",
      "content": "- Introduced by Carolus Linnaeus."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l9x5ha5",
      "content": "- Each organism has two names – Genus and Species."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "17jd04b",
      "content": "- Genus name starts with capital letter."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hdbg81r",
      "content": "- Species name starts with small letter."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0hc00vq",
      "content": "- Names are written in italics when printed."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p88tke8",
      "content": "- Names are underlined separately when handwritten."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "edvb5hd",
      "content": "<strong>10. Biological Measurement Units</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pvcqv3m",
      "content": "- 1 millimeter (mm) = 10^-3 meter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "49zu285",
      "content": "- 1 micrometer (µm) = 10^-6 meter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ash787l",
      "content": "- 1 nanometer (nm) = 10^-9 meter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cc5on4m",
      "content": "- Size of bacteria: 0.5 – 5 µm"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1oi9ux6",
      "content": "- Size of virus: 20 – 300 nm"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "tklth4q",
      "content": "<strong>11. Viruses – Basic Concept</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fdh4dek",
      "content": "Viruses are non-cellular infectious agents that can reproduce only inside a living host cell. They show characteristics of both living and non-living things."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7g6jbg0",
      "content": "- Composed of genetic material (DNA or RNA) and protein coat."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k52i0su",
      "content": "- Outside host – inactive (non-living nature)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "143gk1e",
      "content": "- Inside host – active and reproduce (living nature)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uu84wwt",
      "content": "- Example: HIV, Influenza virus, Coronavirus."
    },
    {
      "id": "kj7edne",
      "type": "heading",
